    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Matthew Perry's dating history: All his girlfriends and relationships\ndate: 2023-10-30\n---\nMatthew Perry's dating history: All his girlfriends and relationships\n\nFrom brief flings with Gwyneth Paltrow and Julia Roberts in the '90s to a failed engagement with Molly Hurwitz in the 2020s, Matthew Perry dated several women inside and outside Hollywood.\n\nThe \"Friends\" star candidly discussed the biggest loves of his life \u2014 as well as his struggles with addiction \u2014 in his memoir, \"Friends, Lovers and the Big Terrible Thing,\" which was released one year before his untimely death in October 2023 at the age of 54.\n\nTake a look back at everyone Perry was romantically linked to through the years on his quest to find \"The One.\"\n\nGwyneth Paltrow\n\n1994\n\nIn his book, Perry described having a brief \"makeout session in a closet\" with Gwyneth Paltrow the summer before \"Friends\" premiered in 1994.\n\nThe actress later shared that she had met Perry at the Williamstown Theatre Festival in Massachusetts.\n\n\"We were both there for most of the summer doing plays. He was so funny and so sweet and so much fun to be with. We drove out to swim in creeks, had beers in the local college bar, kissed in a field of long grass. It was a magical summer. He had shot the pilot of Friends but it had not aired yet. He was nervous, hoping his big break was just around the corner. It was,\" she wrote on Instagram.\n\n\"We stayed friends for a while until we drifted apart, but I was always happy to see him when I did.\"\n\nJulia Roberts\n\n1995-1996\n\nPerry had his first high-profile relationship with none other than Julia Roberts.\n\nThe sitcom star said he and the \"Pretty Woman\" star started dating around the time she made a cameo in a 1995 episode of \"Friends,\" but he broke things off after just two months because he felt like he would \"never be enough\" for her.\n\n\"Dating Julia Roberts had been too much for me. I had been constantly certain that she was going to break up with me,\" Perry wrote in his book, noting that he felt Roberts was \"slumming it\" by dating him.\n\nYasmine Bleeth\n\n1996\n\nSometimes life imitates art: Perry's \"Friends\" character, Chandler Bing, had a crush on Yasmine Bleeth following her turn"
